From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aswin-mcw <aswin.kalies@multicorewareinc.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 17:07:35 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 29/29] aarch64: mingw: emit d-form register names for
 .seh_save_freg

seh_emit_save printed the FP register with aarch64_print_reg, which
renders it from the RTL mode and so produces the v-form ("v15").  The
SEH directives take d-form names: upstream gas keys .seh_save_freg on
.reg_type = 'd' with .reg_addend = 8, matching the Microsoft ARM64
unwind spec where SAVE_FREG covers d8-d15.

winnt.cc was already inconsistent with itself -- seh_pattern_emit prints
"d%ld" for the paired .seh_save_fregp variants while seh_emit_save
printed the v-form for the single-register case.

This never surfaced before because our own gas accepted either spelling:
it read the register number and ignored the letter, so v15 and d15
assembled to byte-identical unwind data.  Upstream's SEH rewrite
(17afc47d8bc), which supersedes our gas SEH commits, validates the letter
and rejects the v-form:

  {standard input}:30556: Error: unexpected register name

Building libstdc++ hits it in floating_to_chars.cc and floating_from_chars.cc.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 gcc/config/mingw/winnt.cc | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gcc/config/mingw/winnt.cc b/gcc/config/mingw/winnt.cc
index 5b728fa405b..742d46358dd 100644
--- a/gcc/config/mingw/winnt.cc
+++ b/gcc/config/mingw/winnt.cc
@@ -1084,7 +1084,12 @@ seh_emit_save (FILE *f, struct seh_frame_state *seh,
   fputs ((FP_REGNUM_P (regno) ? " \t.seh_save_freg\t"
 	 : GP_REGNUM_P (regno) ?  " \t.seh_save_reg\t"
 	 : (gcc_unreachable (), "")), f);
-  aarch64_print_reg (reg, 0, f);
+  /* SEH takes d-form names for FP regs (d8-d15), not the mode-derived
+     v-form; seh_pattern_emit below already prints "d%ld".  */
+  if (FP_REGNUM_P (regno))
+    fprintf (f, "d%d", regno - V0_REGNUM);
+  else
+    aarch64_print_reg (reg, 0, f);
   fprintf (f, ", " HOST_WIDE_INT_PRINT_DEC " \n", abs (cfa_offset));
   return;
 #endif
